1. PROJECT IDENTITY AND PURPOSE
==================================================

Product name: Saivibronics Patient Management Platform.

Organisation: Sri Sathya Sai Organisation.

Initial pilot location: Padmanabhanagar, Bengaluru, Karnataka, India, PIN 560070.

Future scope: Multiple clinics, with a shared platform and carefully separated clinic data.

Primary purpose:

Build a digital platform that helps community members discover participating clinics, register as patients, manage appointments, access their authorised healthcare records and interact with practitioners.

The platform must also support practitioners managing consultations, clinic administrators managing daily operations, and organisation administrators overseeing participating clinics.

The product must support gradual digitisation of historical paper records.

The application must work well on desktop computers, tablets and smartphones. The website should be installable as a Progressive Web App where supported.

The architecture must leave a practical path for a future Android application that can reuse the backend APIs and business rules.

The intended users include senior citizens and people with limited experience using digital services.

The design must therefore prioritise simplicity, clarity, trust, readability and predictable navigation.

This is a healthcare administration and patient management platform. Do not introduce autonomous diagnosis or claim that software-generated recommendations replace qualified clinical judgement.

Use fictional data during development. Do not use actual patient information until the organisation has approved the deployment, security controls, privacy practices and data-handling procedures.

